    License :: Apache License, Version 2.0

    Bilateral ankle exoskeleton: a shank-mounted actuator drives a six-bar
    linkage via cable.

    Level 2: unlike the L1 devices, this is a closed
    kinematic chain.  Five hinges per side, one net degree of freedom, and the
    loop is closed by <equality type="joint"> couplings declared in L2config.yaml
    rather than by the body tree, because MuJoCo's tree cannot express a closed
    loop. The same mechanism ties the linkage to the biological ankle: there is no weld
    or connect between the foot plate and the shoe, only the coupling from
    shank__link_ag to ankle_angle.
====================================================== -->
